    <p>This translation is provided for convenience: the French version prevails.</p>

    <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
    <p>These terms of use govern the use of Movie Marathon, a service that proposes sequences of cinema showtimes ("programmes") based on the schedules published by Pathé. By creating an account or using the service, you accept these terms.</p>

    <h2>2. Publisher</h2>
    <p>The service is published by TDUTRION SOLUTIONS, identified in the <a href="{{ path('app_legal_notice') }}">legal notice</a>.</p>

    <h2>3. Access to the service</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>The service is free of charge. Internet connection costs remain yours.</li>
        <li>It is reserved for signed-in users. Signing in goes through an identity provider (for example Google or GitHub): Movie Marathon neither knows nor stores any password.</li>
        <li>You agree to use an account that belongs to you and not to impersonate anyone.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How it works, and its limits</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Programmes are computed from the schedules published by Pathé, updated regularly. They are given for information only: a showtime may change or be cancelled between two updates.</li>
        <li>Travel times between cinemas are estimated as the crow flies, for the chosen travel mode, regardless of traffic or public transport schedules.</li>
        <li>Tickets are booked and paid for only on the Pathé website, under its own terms. Movie Marathon takes no part in the sale.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Your commitments</h2>
